course: dictionary
lesson: 15498
title: Stunted: growth held back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sometimes a plant, an animal or a person does not grow as big as it should. We say it is stunted. Stunted means smaller or shorter than normal because growth has been slowed or stopped.
explain: Something is usually holding the growth back, such as poor food, illness or a hard place to live. «The tree on the windy cliff was stunted and bent.» The tree did not grow tall because the wind and thin soil held it back.
explain: The word can also describe something that has not developed properly. «The project had stunted progress, so it never got finished.» Ask yourself: what stopped it from growing or moving on? That is the clue to the meaning.
fact: Stunted means smaller or shorter than normal because growth has been slowed or stopped.
fact: Stunt is the verb, and stunted is its past form: stunt, stunts, stunted, stunting.
fact: In science, plants can become stunted if they get too little light, water or nutrients, which pupils test in fair tests.
fact: Stunted growth in children can happen when they do not get enough good food over a long time.
fact: A good check is to swap in "smaller than it should be" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The seedlings were stunted because they had no light.» What does stunted mean here? | Bright green and shiny | Very wet and heavy | *Smaller than normal because growth was held back | Taller and stronger than the others
exercise: «The stunted bush had only three small leaves.» Which clue shows the bush did not grow normally? | The bush had a bright red flower | *Only three small leaves | The bush was very old and famous | The bush was next to the river
exercise: Ella reads that children can have stunted growth without enough good food. Why might that happen? | *They do not get enough good food over a long time | They eat too many vegetables | They sleep too much at night | They play outside every day
test: In a plant test, which would most likely make the plants stunted? | Putting them in the sunshine every day | *Giving them almost no water | Giving them fresh, rich soil | Giving them plenty of water and light
test: «Our stony field gave the sheep stunted grass.» Which meaning fits stunted best? | Wet and cold | Tall, thick and healthy | Coloured bright blue | *Short, because growth was held back
exam: Which phrase means growth that has been slowed or stopped? | Fast-moving growth | Golden growth | Bright, shiny growth | *Stunted growth
